  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n\n## Context\nReview of pull request #464 found that `backend/services/semprec-ai-gateway/src/__tests__/audioHandler.test.ts`'s `it.each` malformed-base64 block (currently around lines 256-274) only posts to `/internal/diarize`. Both `/internal/diarize` (`audioHandler.ts` line 136) and `/internal/transcribe` (`audioHandler.ts` line 166) funnel through the same `validateBody` (defined at line 78), but no equivalent malformed-base64 case exists for `/internal/transcribe`.\n\n## Task\n- Extend (or duplicate, parameterized by endpoint) the malformed-base64 `it.each` block in `audioHandler.test.ts` to also cover `POST /internal/transcribe`, asserting the same validation-failure behavior already asserted for `/internal/diarize`.\n\n## Touches\n- backend/services/semprec-ai-gateway/src/__tests__/audioHandler.test.ts (the malformed-base64 `it.each` block only)\n\n## Scope\n### In scope\n- Extending the named test block to also cover `/internal/transcribe`.\n\n### Out of scope\n- Any other test case or endpoint in `audioHandler.test.ts`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A malformed-base64 request to `POST /internal/transcribe` is asserted to fail validation the same way `/internal/diarize` already is.\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=464 key=8b268b7d54 -->",
